Hypertext Transfer Protocol

HTTP is an application-layer protocol used for web communication.

Traditional HTTP commonly uses:

TCP port 80

HTTP requests can contain methods such as:

GET
POST
PUT
DELETE
HEAD
GET

Requests a resource.

Example:

GET /index.html HTTP/1.1
POST

Sends data to a server.

HTTP Response Codes
Code	Meaning
200	OK / successful
